{"senses": [{"examples": [{"text": "Sī versūs hōrum duōrum poetārum neglegētis, magnā parte litterārum carēbitis.", "bold_text_offsets": [[10, 15]], "translation": "If you neglect the verses of these two poets, you will miss a great part of literature.", "english": "If you neglect the verses of these two poets, you will miss a great part of literature.", "bold_translation_offsets": [[26, 34]], "type": "example"}, {"text": "Hanc rem pūblicam salvam esse volumus.", "bold_text_offsets": [[0, 4]], "translation": "We wish this republic to be safe.", "english": "We wish this republic to be safe.", "bold_translation_offsets": [[8, 12]], "type": "example"}], "links": [["this", "this"], ["these", "these"]], "glosses": ["this; these (in the plural)"], "categories": ["Latin terms with usage examples"], "tags": ["declension-1", "declension-2", "determiner"]}], "pos": "det", "head_templates": [{"name": "la-det", "args": {"1": "hic"}, "expansion": "hic (feminine haec, neuter hoc); first/second-declension determiner (hic-type)"}], "categories": ["Latin 1-syllable words", "Latin adverbs", "Latin determiners", "Latin entries with etymology trees", "Latin entries with etymon", "Latin entries with incorrect language header", "Latin first and second declension determiners", "Latin first and second declension pronouns", "Latin lemmas", "Latin links with manual fragments", "Latin links with redundant alt parameters", "Latin pronouns", "Latin terms derived from Proto-Indo-European", "Latin terms derived from Proto-Italic", "Latin terms derived from the Proto-Indo-European word *ḱe", "Latin terms inherited from Proto-Italic", "Latin terms with IPA pronunciation", "Latin uncomparable adverbs", "Pages using etymon with no ID", "Pages with 8 entries", "Pages with entries", "Pages with etymology trees", "Pages with etymon", "Pages with inline etymon for redlinks"], "forms": [{"form": "haec", "tags": ["feminine"]}, {"form": "hoc", "tags": ["neuter"]}, {"form": "īc", "tags": ["alternative"]}], "etymology_number": "1", "wikipedia": ["Lexikon der indogermanischen Partikeln und Pronominalstämme"], "etymology_text": "Etymology tree\nProto-Indo-European *gʰo\nProto-Italic *ho\nProto-Indo-European *ḱe\nProto-Italic *ke\nProto-Italic *hoke\nLatin hec\nLatin hic\nFrom older hec, from Proto-Italic *hoke, from *ho (from Proto-Indo-European *gʰo (“indeed”, emphatic clitic)) + *ke (from *ḱe (“here”, deictic particle)). Reconstructed forms with o are made likely by the Old Latin form hoi (“this”).\nThe feminine and neuter inflected forms were created in analogy to quī, quae, quod. In the Italic languages only Faliscan has a clear cognate inflected pronoun: hac (acc./abl. sg. f.). A petrified form may be present in the Umbrian word for \"the same\": eru-hu (abl. sg. m.), era-hunt ~ era-font (abl. sg. f.)\nIn Indo-European the first element is cognate with Sanskrit घ (gha) ~ ह (ha, intensifier), हि (hi, “surely, for”), Czech že (“that”, conjunction), Russian же (že, intensifying particle). The second element is cognate with Latin cis (“on this side”), ce-dō, Ancient Greek ἐ-κε-ῖνος (e-ke-înos, “that”), Old Irish cē (“here”), Gothic 𐌷𐌹𐌼𐌼𐌰 (himma, “to this”). More at he, here.", "etymology_links": [["*gʰo", "Reconstruction:Proto-Indo-European/gʰe"], ["*ho", "Reconstruction:Proto-Italic/ho"], ["*ḱe", "Reconstruction:Proto-Indo-European/ḱe#Proto-Indo-European:_here"], ["*ke", "Reconstruction:Proto-Italic/ke"], ["*hoke", "Reconstruction:Proto-Italic/hoke"], ["hec", "hec#Latin"], ["hec", "hec#Latin"], ["*ho", "Reconstruction:Proto-Italic/ho"], ["*gʰo", "Reconstruction:Proto-Indo-European/gʰe"], ["*ke", "Reconstruction:Proto-Italic/ke"], ["*ḱe", "Reconstruction:Proto-Indo-European/ḱe"], ["hoi", "hoi#Latin:_pronoun"], ["quī, quae, quod", "hic#Latin"], ["hac", "hac#Faliscan"], ["eru-hu", "eruhu#Umbrian"], ["era-hunt ~ era-font", "erahunt#Umbrian"], ["घ", "घ#Sanskrit"], ["ह", "ह#Sanskrit:_emphatic_particle"], ["हि", "हि#Sanskrit"], ["že", "že#Czech"], ["же", "же#Russian"], ["cis", "cis#Latin"], ["ce-dō", "cedo#Latin"], ["ἐ-κε-ῖνος", "ἐκεῖνος#Ancient_Greek"], ["cē", "ce#Old_Irish"], ["𐌷𐌹𐌼𐌼𐌰", "𐌷𐌹𐌼𐌼𐌰#Gothic"], ["he", "he#English"], ["here", "here#English"]], "etymology_templates": [{"name": "ety", "args": {"1": "la", "id": "this", "2": ":from", "3": "hec<ety:inh<itc-pro:*hoke<ety:af<*ho><*ke>>>>", "tree": "1"}, "expansion": "Etymology tree\nProto-Indo-European *gʰo\nProto-Italic *ho\nProto-Indo-European *ḱe\nProto-Italic *ke\nProto-Italic *hoke\nLatin hec\nLatin hic\n[Appendix:Glossary#inherited|Inherited]] from\", \"keyword\" : \"inherited\" } ], \"lang_name\" : \"Proto-Italic\", \"term\" : \"*ho\", \"status\" : \"ok\", \"lang\" : \"itc-pro\" }, { \"children\" : [ { \"terms\" : [ { \"id\" : \"here\", \"children\" : [ ], \"status\" : \"ok\", \"lang_name\" : \"Proto-Indo-European\", \"term\" : \"*ḱe\", \"lang\" : \"ine-pro\" } ], \"keyword_label\" : \"Inherited from\", \"keyword\" : \"inherited\" } ], \"lang_name\" : \"Proto-Italic\", \"term\" : \"*ke\", \"status\" : \"ok\", \"lang\" : \"itc-pro\" } ], \"keyword_label\" : \"From\", \"is_group\" : true, \"keyword\" : \"affix\" } ], \"lang_name\" : \"Proto-Italic\", \"term\" : \"*hoke\", \"status\" : \"inline\", \"lang\" : \"itc-pro\" } ], \"keyword_label\" : \"Inherited from\", \"keyword\" : \"inherited\" } ], \"lang_name\" : \"Latin\", \"term\" : \"hec\", \"status\" : \"inline\", \"lang\" : \"la\" } ], \"keyword_label\" : \"From\", \"keyword\" : \"from\" } ], \"status\" : \"ok\", \"lang_name\" : \"Latin\", \"term\" : \"hic\", \"lang\" : \"la\" }\" data-id=\"this\" data-lang=\"la\" data-title=\"hic\" id=\"Latin:_this\">"}, {"name": "inh", "args": {"1": "la", "2": "itc-pro", "3": "", "4": "*hoke"}, "expansion": "Proto-Italic *hoke"}, {"name": "der", "args": {"1": "la", "2": "ine-pro", "3": "*gʰe", "4": "*gʰo", "t": "indeed", "pos": "emphatic clitic"}, "expansion": "Proto-Indo-European *gʰo (“indeed”, emphatic clitic)"}, {"name": "cog", "args": {"1": "sa", "2": "घ"}, "expansion": "Sanskrit घ (gha)"}, {"name": "cog", "args": {"1": "cs", "2": "že", "3": "", "4": "that", "pos": "conjunction"}, "expansion": "Czech že (“that”, conjunction)"}, {"name": "cog", "args": {"1": "ru", "2": "же", "3": "", "pos": "intensifying particle"}, "expansion": "Russian же (že, intensifying particle)"}, {"name": "cog", "args": {"1": "la", "2": "cis", "3": "", "4": "on this side"}, "expansion": "Latin cis (“on this side”)"}, {"name": "cog", "args": {"1": "grc", "2": "ἐκεῖνος", "3": "ἐ-κε-ῖνος", "4": "that"}, "expansion": "Ancient Greek ἐ-κε-ῖνος (e-ke-înos, “that”)"}, {"name": "cog", "args": {"1": "sga", "2": "ce", "3": "cē", "4": "here"}, "expansion": "Old Irish cē (“here”)"}, {"name": "cog", "args": {"1": "got", "2": "𐌷𐌹𐌼𐌼𐌰", "3": "", "4": "to this"}, "expansion": "Gothic 𐌷𐌹𐌼𐌼𐌰 (himma, “to this”)"}], "sounds": [{"tags": ["Classical-Latin"], "ipa": "[ˈhɪk]"}, {"note": "modern Italianate Ecclesiastical", "ipa": "[ˈik]"}], "word": "hic", "lang": "Latin", "lang_code": "la"}
{"senses": [{"examples": [{"text": "Mitte hunc meā grātiā.", "bold_text_offsets": [[6, 10]], "translation": "Let him alone for my sake.", "english": "Let him alone for my sake.", "bold_translation_offsets": [[4, 7]], "type": "example"}, {"text": "[...] Miserae hoc tamen ūnum / exsequere, Anna, mihī. [...].", "ref": "29 BCE – 19 BCE, Vergilius, Aeneis 4.420–421", "english": "[Dido speaks:] “Nevertheless, carry out this one [request], Anna, for [your] unfortunate [sister].”", "translation": "[Dido speaks:] “Nevertheless, carry out this one [request], Anna, for [your] unfortunate [sister].”", "type": "quotation"}, {"text": "Hōrum tē morī nēmō cōget, omnēs docēbunt; hōrum nēmō annōs tuōs conteret, suōs tibi contribuet; nūllīus ex hīs sermō perīculōsus erit, nūllīus amīcitia capitālis, nūllīus sūmptuōsa observātiō.", "ref": "c. 4 BCE – 65 CE, Seneca Minor, De brevitate vitae 15", "english": "No one of these will force you to die, but all will teach you how to die; no one of these will wear out your years, but each will add his own years to yours; nothing from these conversations will bring you peril, the friendship of none will endanger your life, the courting of none will tax your purse.", "translation": "No one of these will force you to die, but all will teach you how to die; no one of these will wear out your years, but each will add his own years to yours; nothing from these conversations will bring you peril, the friendship of none will endanger your life, the courting of none will tax your purse.", "type": "quotation"}, {"text": "hīs dea plācanda est", "ref": "8 CE, Ovidius, Fasti 4.777", "english": "With these [supplications] must the goddess be appeased", "translation": "With these [supplications] must the goddess be appeased", "type": "quotation"}], "links": [["this", "this"], ["one", "one"], ["this", "this"], ["these", "these"], ["one", "one"], ["these", "these"], ["he", "he"], ["she", "she"], ["it", "it"]], "categories": ["Latin terms with quotations", "Latin